.DS_Store
.obsidian/
RAM-USB.md
RAM-USB/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
graphify-out/

# Generated dev-only TLS key material (third-party/entry-hub/generate-dev-cert.sh,
# third-party/headscale/dev-tls/README.txt's openssl command) -
# real key bytes, regenerated on demand, never committed (unlike the
# zero-entropy *.dev-only.txt placeholder files elsewhere under third-party/).
# The headscale key was committed by mistake on 2026-07-16 (found via
# gitleaks 2026-07-20) - inconsistent with this same rule already applied
# to entry-hub's equivalent; tracking removed via `git rm --cached`, see
# git-agent's advisory for the exact commit.
third-party/entry-hub/config/*.dev-only.*
third-party/headscale/dev-tls/*.dev-only.pem

# third-party/headscale/ca-root/: RAM-USB's internal Certificate-Authority
# root certificate, extracted as a plain file (docker cp) by
# deployments/scripts/headscale.sh so nginx can trust it for NM-F-12's
# client-certificate verification - this container has no pkg/pki
# bootstrap flow of its own to obtain it through. Not a private key, but
# still regenerated fresh on every run, same convention as every other
# dev-only extracted artifact in this project.
third-party/headscale/ca-root/*.dev-only.crt

# third-party/mosquitto/generate-dev-certs.sh's output: the real
# Certificate-Authority's root cert (copied verbatim) plus a real-CA-issued
# broker cert and one real-CA-issued client cert per publishing/
# subscribing identity - real key bytes, regenerated on demand (and, since
# these are real-CA-issued leaf certificates, ~24h-lived - regeneration is
# expected routinely, not just occasionally), never committed, same
# convention as the entries above.
third-party/mosquitto/certs/*.dev-only.*
third-party/mosquitto/certs/*.srl

# Real dev-only master key/pepper/CA bootstrap tokens generated while
# manually verifying the full stack against a real running Certificate-
# Authority (2026-07-20 real-CA end-to-end test) - never committed.
deployments/.env.realca-test
deployments/.env.local

# ThesisAtUniud/: LaTeX build artifacts from pdflatex/bibtex/latexmk -
# regenerated on every compile, never committed. Same convention as the
# THUD template's own original .gitignore. The Makefile's thesis/thesis-no-dedica
# targets put these under ThesisAtUniud/build/with-dedica/ and
# ThesisAtUniud/build/no-dedica/ respectively; the patterns below also still catch
# stray output from a manual, non-Makefile pdflatex/latexmk run in ThesisAtUniud/
# itself. build/with-dedica/ is ignored wholesale — it never holds anything meant
# to be shared. Inside build/no-dedica/, everything is ignored except
# thesis_Verrengia_no-dedica.pdf itself, tracked deliberately so it can be shared
# (e.g. with the thesis supervisor) without exposing the dedication/ringraziamenti.
# Each directory on the path to that one exception must be explicitly un-ignored
# ("!dir/") for git to even look inside it — a "dir/*" (not "dir/") ignore alone
# stops git from descending into it at all, which is why this cascades one level
# at a time instead of a single top-level pattern.
ThesisAtUniud/build/*
!ThesisAtUniud/build/no-dedica/
ThesisAtUniud/build/no-dedica/*
!ThesisAtUniud/build/no-dedica/thesis_Verrengia_no-dedica.pdf
ThesisAtUniud/*.aux
ThesisAtUniud/*.bbl
ThesisAtUniud/*.blg
ThesisAtUniud/*.log
ThesisAtUniud/*.out
ThesisAtUniud/*.pdf
ThesisAtUniud/*.synctex.gz
ThesisAtUniud/*.toc
ThesisAtUniud/*.lof
ThesisAtUniud/*.lot
ThesisAtUniud/*.fls
ThesisAtUniud/*.fdb_latexmk
ThesisAtUniud/pdfa.xmpi
ThesisAtUniud/no-dedica.flag

# ThesisAtUniud/chapters/00_*: personal dedication and acknowledgements text,
# kept out of the public commit history.
ThesisAtUniud/chapters/00_dedica.tex
ThesisAtUniud/chapters/00_ringraziamenti.tex

# ThesisAtUniud/chapters/Bozze.tex: scratch/draft notes, not thesis content.
ThesisAtUniud/chapters/Bozze.tex

# ThesisAtUniud/references/: local copies of copyrighted papers kept for
# personal citation-verification, never redistributed in a public repo.
ThesisAtUniud/references/
